# jobcrawler — deployment environment (§11)
#
# Copy to a real path the systemd unit reads (e.g. /etc/jobcrawler/jobcrawler.env),
# fill in the three REQUIRED values, then `chmod 600` it — it holds an API key.
#
# This file enumerates the FULL env surface (every JOBCRAWLER_* getter in
# src/jobcrawler/config.py), grouped by subsystem the same way that module is.
# Only the REQUIRED block is uncommented; every other line is commented out and
# shows the built-in default — uncomment one only to override it. The defaults are
# tuned for a job tracker (boards move on the order of days, not minutes), so an
# untouched copy runs sanely; ../README.md carries the operator prose.
#
# ONE MORE required input, not an env var: PROFILE.md (see JOBCRAWLER_PROFILE
# below). The §4.6 matcher scores every new position against it; with no profile
# the daemon has nothing to match, so it fails loud rather than scoring blind.

# --- REQUIRED ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Provider API key for the LM. The model slug's `openrouter/` prefix tells
# litellm to read OPENROUTER_API_KEY (use OPENAI_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# instead if you point the model slugs at those providers). Read by litellm,
# not by the app's own config — so it never appears in `jobcrawl`'s env table.
# Needed by `generate`/`optimize` AND by `run`: the §4.6 host-side matcher scores
# new positions with a (cheap) LM, so a running daemon bills match tokens even
# though the committed crawl loop itself never calls an LM. NOT needed if every
# configured slug is `chatgpt/*` (see the ChatGPT-subscription OAuth section below).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-REPLACE_ME

# RLM root planner/extractor — a strong, code-capable model. No default: an
# unset value fails loud at generate/optimize rather than 404-ing deep in the
# provider. Used only by `generate`/`optimize`; the crawl loop never calls it.
JOBCRAWLER_MODEL=openrouter/<vendor>/<strong-code-model>

# RLM sub_lm — a cheaper code-capable model for in-sandbox llm_query. Required:
# unset, every in-sandbox query silently bills at the root planner's rate. Also
# the §4.6 matcher's fallback model (see JOBCRAWLER_MATCH_MODEL) — so on a `run`
# host that only crawls+matches, this is the one model slug you must set.
JOBCRAWLER_SUB_MODEL=openrouter/<vendor>/<cheap-code-model>

# --- PROFILE & MATCHER (§4.6) — the only host-side LLM surface ---------------
# The profile matcher scores each new position against PROFILE.md, host-side and
# OUTSIDE the crawl sandbox: batched into one LLM call per JOBCRAWLER_MATCH_BATCH
# jobs and cached by (content, profile, model, prompt) so an unchanged job is
# never re-billed. Every knob here bounds that surface's token spend or strictness.

# Path to PROFILE.md — YAML frontmatter (machine prefs: disciplines/levels/
# workplace/locations/min_salary/exclude_*) between `---` fences, then a free
# markdown body handed verbatim to the match LM. CWD-relative default resolves to
# /data/PROFILE.md in the container (WorkingDir=/data) and is set absolutely by the
# native unit. Keep it on the persistent volume beside sites.yaml — editing it
# lazily re-scores affected jobs (the file's hash keys the match cache).
#JOBCRAWLER_PROFILE=PROFILE.md

# Dedicated match LM. Optional — unset, matching borrows JOBCRAWLER_SUB_MODEL
# (the cheap fallback). It deliberately NEVER falls back to the root planner
# (JOBCRAWLER_MODEL), whose per-token rate would make scoring the daily fleet
# ruinous. Set this only to run matching on a model distinct from the sub_lm.
#JOBCRAWLER_MATCH_MODEL=openrouter/<vendor>/<cheap-match-model>

# Jobs per single MatchJobs LLM call. Batching amortizes the profile+rubric prompt
# prefix (the dominant cost) across many compact job digests; too large and one
# malformed batch response strands more jobs to match_pending. Default 10.
#JOBCRAWLER_MATCH_BATCH=10

# 0-100 score at/above which a match is worth an operator notification ('match'
# event). NOT a drop — the matcher scores everything and stores the verdict; a 60
# still lands in the store's match view, it just doesn't ping. Default 70.
#JOBCRAWLER_MATCH_MIN_SCORE=70

# Hard per-UTC-day ceiling on jobs sent to the match LM — the token-budget
# backstop. Cache hits are FREE and never counted. Jobs past the cap are marked
# match_pending (drained by later runs / the recheck loop), NEVER dropped. Bounds
# a fresh-profile rematch storm or a big first crawl from blowing the day. Def 400.
#JOBCRAWLER_MATCH_DAILY_CAP=400

# Governor pacing for the match LM (requests/interval) so a big new-position sweep
# can't burst the provider into rate limits. Paces CALLS; orthogonal to the DAILY
# cap which bounds VOLUME. Same grammar as JOBCRAWLER_RATE_LIMIT. Default 10/m.
#JOBCRAWLER_MATCH_RATE=10/m

# On a site's FIRST position-yielding crawl, only the newest N jobs (by posted_at)
# go to the matcher now; the backlog tail is match_pending and drained later. A
# fresh board can list hundreds of standing roles — this keeps a first crawl from
# burning the whole daily cap on stale backlog. Default 30.
#JOBCRAWLER_FIRST_CRAWL_CAP=30

# --- OPTIONAL: GEPA reflection model (§4.11) --------------------------------

# GEPA reflection model for `jobcrawl optimize`. Ideally a strong model from a
# *different* family than JOBCRAWLER_MODEL. Only needed if you run optimize.
#JOBCRAWLER_REFLECTION_MODEL=anthropic/<strong-model>

# --- OPTIONAL: ChatGPT-subscription OAuth (§9) ------------------------------
# Any model slug above may be `chatgpt/<model>` (e.g. chatgpt/gpt-5-codex) to bill
# against a ChatGPT Plus/Pro subscription via the Codex Responses backend instead
# of per-token OpenRouter credits — then OPENROUTER_API_KEY is not needed for that
# slug. jobcrawler writes NO OAuth flow: run the official `codex login` once (it
# does the browser flow, writes ~/.codex/auth.json), then `jobcrawl login` imports
# that token here; litellm reads and refreshes it. `run`/`crawl` fail fast at
# startup if a chatgpt/* slug has no usable token (never a blocking prompt). Note
# this backend prepends the Codex coding-agent system prompt to every request.
#
# Where jobcrawl login stores the imported token (a token store, not an API key —
# `chmod 600` it). Falls back to litellm's own CHATGPT_TOKEN_DIR, then this default.
#JOBCRAWLER_AUTH_DIR=~/.config/jobcrawler/chatgpt

# --- OBSERVABILITY (§4.9) ---------------------------------------------------

# Daemon log verbosity (DEBUG|INFO|WARNING|ERROR). Default INFO.
#JOBCRAWLER_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# Webhook POSTed a small JSON payload on every autonomous action (heal/promote,
# adopt, generator rollback) AND on a strong profile match, alongside the log
# line. Best-effort, fire-and-forget. Unset ⇒ log only.
#JOBCRAWLER_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK=https://hooks.example.com/jobcrawler
#JOBCRAWLER_NOTIFY_TIMEOUT=10

# --- CLOUDFLARE / SOLVER (§4.10) --------------------------------------------

# Challenge solver backend. Default `none` (plain httpx) — most ATS/JSON job
# boards need no solver. The only built backend is flaresolverr, which requires
# FLARESOLVERR_URL. `render: solver` sites in sites.yaml need this set.
#JOBCRAWLER_SOLVER=none
#FLARESOLVERR_URL=http://flaresolverr:8191/v1
#JOBCRAWLER_CLEARANCE_TTL=30m
# Route live fetches through an outbound HTTP proxy (unset ⇒ direct).
#JOBCRAWLER_EGRESS_PROXY=http://proxy:3128

# --- SCHEDULER & ADAPTIVE CADENCE (§4.9) ------------------------------------
# Job-tracker defaults are far slower than the old news cadence: boards move on
# the order of days, so hitting one every few hours catches a posting the day it
# lands while staying polite.

# Fixed cadence for a site with no `schedule:` and adaptive off. Default 4h.
#JOBCRAWLER_DEFAULT_SCHEDULE=4h
# How many sites crawl at once (global semaphore). Default 4.
#JOBCRAWLER_CONCURRENCY=4
# Adaptive politeness floor / staleness ceiling — an adaptive site's learned
# interval is clamped into this band. Jobs don't churn minute-to-minute and a role
# stays open for weeks, so 1h..3d (was 15m..1d for news).
#JOBCRAWLER_MIN_SCHEDULE=1h
#JOBCRAWLER_MAX_SCHEDULE=3d
# A site with no explicit schedule self-tunes its cadence to its hit-rate rather
# than using the fixed default. Default true; pin `schedule:`/`adaptive: false`
# on a site to opt out.
#JOBCRAWLER_ADAPTIVE_DEFAULT=true
# Adaptive controller: desired checks-per-post (steers hit rate to 1/N) and how
# many recent crawls it averages over. Defaults 2 and 8.
#JOBCRAWLER_ADAPTIVE_TARGET_N=2
#JOBCRAWLER_ADAPTIVE_WINDOW=8

# --- POSITION LIFECYCLE: closure & recheck (§4.7, §4.9) ---------------------
# How an open position ages into 'closed', and how sources that don't enumerate
# their whole board (enumerates_all: false — an RSS/latest-N feed) get re-verified.

# Consecutive crawls a position must be ABSENT from an ENUMERATING board before it
# is closed. Default 2: one miss is often a transient hiccup (a dropped page, an
# ATS 500) and only increments missing_streak; the second confirms it's gone. Only
# enumerating sources diff this way, and only after a successful, non-empty crawl
# (the §4.7 mass-closure guard) — so this can never mass-close on a failed fetch.
#JOBCRAWLER_CLOSE_AFTER_MISSES=2

# How often the recheck loop re-fetches standing open positions to confirm they're
# still live. This is the ONLY closure signal for non-enumerating sources (RSS /
# latest-N, where the diff is unsound); it also re-checks enumerating rows against
# the expired-markers / expires_at. Default 12h. `off` disables it.
#JOBCRAWLER_RECHECK_INTERVAL=12h
# Max standing positions the recheck loop re-fetches per pass (oldest-checked
# first, so all rows are covered over successive passes). Default 150.
#JOBCRAWLER_RECHECK_CAP=150

# `|`-separated substrings that mark a still-listed posting as already closed
# (an ATS keeps serving "this position has been filled" after the opening is gone;
# the enumerate-diff can't catch it because the URL is still present). A
# description carrying one is dropped at ingest as 'expired'. Empty disables.
# Default (EN + pt-BR): the five below.
#JOBCRAWLER_EXPIRED_MARKERS=no longer accepting applications|this position has been filled|position is no longer available|vaga encerrada|vaga indisponível

# --- COMPLETENESS & GATE THRESHOLDS (§6; host-side, hidden from the generator) ---

# Minimum positions a crawl must yield to clear the completeness gate. Default 1
# (was 5 for news): a two-role startup careers page is a legitimate complete board.
# Completeness is instead carried by the relative enum-floor + stability gates.
#JOBCRAWLER_MIN_ITEMS=1
# Length floor (chars) a job description must clear to count as complete. Default
# 300 (was 400): a tight-but-real posting clears it, a title-only stub does not.
#JOBCRAWLER_MIN_DESCRIPTION_CHARS=300
# Fraction of sampled descriptions that must clear the length floor for the gate
# to pass. Default 0.6 — tolerates a minority of genuinely terse postings.
#JOBCRAWLER_MIN_DESCRIPTION_QUALITY=0.6
# Minimum count of DISTINCT chars a description must contain — catches boilerplate
# padding that clears the length floor but is a repeated blurb / placeholder. 150.
#JOBCRAWLER_MIN_UNIQUE_DESCRIPTION_CHARS=150
# Run-to-run stability (Jaccard) and enum-floor ratio gates (§6). Defaults 0.6/0.5.
#JOBCRAWLER_STABILITY_JACCARD=0.6
#JOBCRAWLER_ENUM_FLOOR_RATIO=0.5

# --- CRAWL / POLITENESS (§4.5) ----------------------------------------------

# Identify the crawler to the boards you fetch. Default `jobcrawler/0.1 (+job tracker)`.
#JOBCRAWLER_USER_AGENT=jobcrawler/0.1 (+job tracker)
# Per-host politeness pacing (requests/interval/scope). Default 1/s/host.
#JOBCRAWLER_RATE_LIMIT=1/s/host
# Hard cap on pages one crawl fetches. Default 200.
#JOBCRAWLER_MAX_PAGES=200
# Per-request HTTP timeout, and transient-failure retry policy (429/503/dropped
# connection): extra attempts, exponential backoff base, and the per-wait ceiling
# (also the longest Retry-After honored). Defaults 20s / 2 / 0.5 / 30s.
#JOBCRAWLER_FETCH_TIMEOUT=20
#JOBCRAWLER_FETCH_RETRIES=2
#JOBCRAWLER_FETCH_BACKOFF=0.5
#JOBCRAWLER_FETCH_RETRY_CAP=30
# Comma-separated tracking query params stripped during URL canonicalization
# (unset ⇒ the built-in utm_*/gclid/... denylist).
#JOBCRAWLER_TRACKING_PARAM_DENYLIST=utm_source,utm_medium,gclid

# --- COMMITTED-CRAWL ISOLATION (§4.4) ---------------------------------------
# A committed crawler runs in an isolated subprocess (rlimits + wall-clock) so a
# runaway one can't take down the daemon.
#JOBCRAWLER_CRAWL_TIMEOUT=600
#JOBCRAWLER_CRAWL_CPU_SECONDS=120
#JOBCRAWLER_CRAWL_MEM_MB=1024

# --- GENERATION CAPS (§4.2; generate/optimize only) -------------------------
#JOBCRAWLER_MAX_ITERATIONS=20
#JOBCRAWLER_MAX_LLM_CALLS=40
#JOBCRAWLER_MAX_SUBCALLS=60
#JOBCRAWLER_FANOUT_SPEND_CAP=$8/site
#JOBCRAWLER_FANOUT_N=4
#JOBCRAWLER_MAX_TOKENS=16000
#JOBCRAWLER_CORPUS_HOMEPAGE_CHARS=60000
#JOBCRAWLER_CORPUS_ARTICLE_CHARS=20000

# --- AUTONOMY: the daemon's self-modification (§4.8 / §4.11 / §8) -----------

# Master kill-switch over every self-modifying action (self-heal, auto-promote,
# reopt dispatch, auto-adopt). Default `on`. Set `off` to freeze the daemon's
# initiative while it keeps crawling/matching; operator commands still work.
#JOBCRAWLER_AUTONOMY=on

# Self-heal & §4.2 cold-start delivery. Default `auto`: a healed or brand-new-site
# crawler is auto-promoted with a _history/ backup (undo via `rollback`). `on`
# stages it for a human `promote` instead; `off` writes live with no backup.
#JOBCRAWLER_REVIEW_GATE=auto

# Periodic staleness sweep cadence and the per-site cooldown on the event-driven
# fast path (a drifted crawl heals immediately, rate-limited by this). `off`
# disables each. Defaults 24h / 6h.
#JOBCRAWLER_REGEN_CHECK=24h
#JOBCRAWLER_HEAL_COOLDOWN=6h
# Share of complete-description positions below which a crawl is a partial-drift
# signal (board started serving title-only stubs). Default 0.5.
#JOBCRAWLER_DESCRIPTION_QUALITY_FLOOR=0.5
# Generation-failed retry backoff: base delay, doubling per consecutive failure up
# to the cap — a chronically broken site backs off without ever giving up. 6h / 7d.
#JOBCRAWLER_GENFAIL_BACKOFF=6h
#JOBCRAWLER_GENFAIL_BACKOFF_CAP=7d

# Offline GEPA self-improvement (§4.11). REOPT_CHECK is how often the scheduler
# *checks* whether to dispatch a compile (a check only dispatches when the
# readiness gates pass — not a daily compile); `off` disables it. Each dispatch
# runs `jobcrawl optimize` detached, single-flighted by the lock, logging to the
# log path. Defaults 24h / optimize.lock / optimize.log.
#JOBCRAWLER_REOPT_CHECK=24h
#JOBCRAWLER_OPTIMIZE_LOCK=optimize.lock
#JOBCRAWLER_OPTIMIZE_LOG=optimize.log
# Trainset stability required before optimize, and held-out eval passes averaged
# before a promotion decision (stochastic generator ⇒ average to de-noise). 3 / 3.
#JOBCRAWLER_TRAINSET_STABLE_RUNS=3
#JOBCRAWLER_PROMOTION_EVAL_PASSES=3
# Post-adoption regression watcher: probation window before it judges a newly
# adopted generator, and how many MORE sites must newly fail generation in the
# window after adoption than before to trigger an auto-rollback. `off` on the
# probation disables the watcher. Defaults 48h / 2.
#JOBCRAWLER_ADOPT_PROBATION=48h
#JOBCRAWLER_ADOPT_REGRESSION_DELTA=2

# --- STATE, REGISTRY & ARTIFACT PATHS ---------------------------------------
# The container image bakes these onto the /data volume and the native unit sets
# them absolutely; override here only for a custom layout. All are persistent —
# the state DB now also holds the positions ledger, the match cache/spend, and the
# §16 operator tracking axis (status/notes/applied-date), shared read/write with
# `jobcrawl serve` via SQLite WAL.
#JOBCRAWLER_SITES=sites.yaml
#JOBCRAWLER_STATE_URL=sqlite:///jobcrawler.db
#JOBCRAWLER_CRAWLERS_DIR=crawlers
#JOBCRAWLER_GENERATOR_DIR=generators
#JOBCRAWLER_GENERATOR_PATH=
#JOBCRAWLER_TRAINSET_PATH=trainset.jsonl

# --- WEB TRACKER (§16; `jobcrawl serve`) ------------------------------------
# The tracker UI is a SEPARATE process from the `run` daemon — start it with
# `jobcrawl serve` (its own systemd unit, or by hand). It reads/writes the same
# state DB above (WAL makes the daemon-writer / UI-writer overlap safe) and runs
# no scheduler and no LLM, so it needs none of the model/API config above.
#
# It binds LOOPBACK by default: the UI exposes personal application data (which
# roles you applied to, private notes), so it must NOT be world-reachable. Set
# 0.0.0.0 only when it sits behind a trusted authenticating reverse proxy — never
# raw on a public interface. Per-invocation flags (`--host`/`--port`) win over these.
#JOBCRAWLER_SERVE_HOST=127.0.0.1
#JOBCRAWLER_SERVE_PORT=8765
